# Warehouse QR Check-in, GPS Queue & Smart Order Assignment — Implementation Plan

## Goal

Build a complete, production-ready system for:
1. **QR/GPS Warehouse Check-in** — riders scan a warehouse QR code, GPS is verified against the warehouse radius before check-in is accepted.
2. **FIFO Rider Queue** — checked-in riders are queued by arrival time; the first rider in queue gets the first order.
3. **Smart Order Assignment** — orders auto-assign only to riders satisfying all eligibility conditions (GPS inside radius, online, no active delivery, vehicle match, same warehouse).
4. **20-Second Accept/Reject Timer** — sequential offer with auto-skip to next queue position.
5. **Auto-Eviction from Queue** — riders removed when they leave radius, go offline, logout, or are inactive.
6. **Queue Monitoring Dashboard** — real-time visibility for Admin and Warehouse staff.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The existing **admin → seller → delivery** order flow is **NOT changed**. This module adds a parallel warehouse-centric rider management layer on top of the existing workflow. The seller step remains intact.

