## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Warehouse–Order Linkage**
> Currently orders are linked to a **seller**, not directly to a warehouse. Should we:
> - **Option A**: Use the warehouse's GPS coordinates to determine which warehouse queue handles the order (closest warehouse to seller location) — **Recommended**
> - **Option B**: Add an explicit `warehouseId` field to orders at placement time
>
> This affects how the order assignment engine picks which warehouse queue to pull from.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: Multi-warehouse rider**
> Can a delivery partner check in to **only one warehouse at a time**, or multiple?
> The plan assumes **one active check-in per rider** at any time.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Vehicle Type Filtering**
> Do orders currently carry a `requiredVehicleType` field? Looking at the Order model — it does not appear to have this field. Should we:
> - **Option A**: Add `requiredVehicleType` to the Order model and let warehouse/seller set it
> - **Option B**: Skip vehicle type filtering for now (all vehicle types eligible)

> [!NOTE]
> **Q4: Inactivity timeout**
> The configurable inactivity timeout — should this be global (admin setting) or per-warehouse? Recommend: admin-level setting with default of 30 minutes.

