## Data Flow Diagram

```
Rider scans QR
     │
     ▼
POST /delivery/warehouse/checkin
  ├─ Verify QR token (HMAC) → warehouseId
  ├─ Fetch rider GPS (from request body)
  ├─ Fetch warehouse location + checkinRadius
  ├─ Haversine distance ≤ checkinRadius? 
  │    NO  → 403 "Outside warehouse radius"
  │    YES ↓
  ├─ Create WarehouseCheckin { deliveryId, warehouseId, checkinTime, status:"active" }
  ├─ Update Delivery { activeCheckinId, activeWarehouseId, queueStatus:"waiting" }
  └─ Emit socket "queue:rider_joined" → warehouse room

         [Every 60s — GPS Watchdog Job]
              │
              ▼
         For each active checkin:
           ├─ Get Delivery.location
           ├─ Haversine check
           ├─ Outside? → checkOutRider("gps_evicted")
           └─ Emit "queue:gps_evicted"

Seller accepts order
     │
     ▼
sellerAcceptAtomic()  ← existing code, no breaking change
     │
     ├─ existing broadcast logic (retained as fallback)
     │
     └─ NEW: find warehouse for this order
              │
              ▼
         offerToNextInQueue(orderId, warehouseId)
              │
              ├─ Get FIFO queue → pick top eligible rider
              ├─ Emit "queue:order_offered" to rider socket
              ├─ Schedule 20s BullMQ job (QUEUE_OFFER_TIMEOUT)
              │
              ├─ Rider accepts within 20s:
              │    └─ deliveryAcceptAtomic() (existing) → order assigned
              │
              └─ Timeout / Reject:
                   └─ offerToNextInQueue(orderId, warehouseId, [skippedIds])
                        └─ If queue exhausted → fallback to broadcast
```

